menu "WIFI 8711 (AT-over-SPI) module"

config WIFI_8711
	bool "External 8711 Wi-Fi chip over SPI"
	default n
	help
	  Enable the AT-over-SPI link toward the external 8711 Wi-Fi chip: the
	  SPI DMA master plus the AT command engine.  TCP/IP lives in the 8711's
	  own firmware, so this brings up no Zephyr net stack.

	  Turned on by the wifi_8711 snippet
	  (applications/eBadge_8773g_8711f/snippets/wifi_8711), which also
	  supplies the wifi_8711_device / wifi_8711_resources / psram1_nc
	  devicetree nodes this module binds to.  Enabling the symbol on its own
	  will not build -- the DT nodes must come with it.

config WIFI_8711_ROLE_MASTER
	bool "SPI master role"
	depends on WIFI_8711
	default y
	help
	  Build the SPI master side (we clock the bus, the 8711 is the slave).
	  This is the only role this product supports; keep it enabled.

config WIFI_8711_TEST
	bool "wifi8711 shell command group"
	depends on WIFI_8711 && SHELL
	default n
	help
	  Register the `wifi8711` shell commands for bring-up: probe the DT
	  bindings, toggle the M2S line, and report link state.  Useful before
	  the eBadge port_softap / port_tcp layers exist.

endmenu
